From bdb9a4cbd85418516d4c78107acc92a3489037fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sisshiki1969 <sisshiki@isshiki-clinic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 04:02:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add an audio interface to the WebAssembly module

doom.wasm produces no sound: its ten imports carry the framebuffer, the
clock, WAD loading, save games and logging, and nothing tells a host that a
sound should be heard. The README lists audio as a wishlist item.

Doom itself needs no change for this. `i_sound.c` already looks for a
`DG_sound_module` / `DG_music_module` pair behind FEATURE_SOUND, and
`i_sound.c` / `s_sound.c` / `sounds.c` are already compiled in; only the
bottom layer, the one that would touch an audio device, was missing. This
adds it as thirteen `audio` imports and the two module structs that
forward to them.

Sample data crosses the boundary once per sound rather than once per play:
`registerSound` hands over a sound's DMX lump the first time it is heard,
and every later `startSound` names it by id alone, so a host never has to
know how a WAD is laid out. Music crosses as standard MIDI, the module
converting Doom's own MUS encoding with the mus2mid that already ships
here, so a host needs a MIDI player rather than a MUS parser. That is also
what the SDL music module does before handing a lump to SDL_mixer.

Three things had to be fixed for FEATURE_SOUND to work at all, none of
which anything exercised while it was never defined:

  * `i_sound.c` declared `extern sound_module_t *DG_sound_module` but used
    `&DG_sound_module` and the SDL module defines it unstarred, so the
    types did not agree.

  * FEATURE_SOUND was doing double duty as "SDL's headers are available":
    it pulled <SDL_mixer.h> into i_sound.c, <SDL_endian.h> into i_swap.h,
    which is endianness handling and not a sound feature at all, and bound
    two config variables that only the SDL sound module defines. A port
    with a sound module but no SDL now says DG_WITHOUT_SDL and gets the
    plain little-endian definitions.

  * `I_PrecacheSounds` runs as the first statement of `S_Init`, before the
    loop that sets each `lumpnum` to -1, so at that point every one is
    still zero -- a real lump (PLAYPAL), not an obviously invalid one. The
    SDL module sidesteps this by resolving every name itself; this module
    registers lazily from `StartSound` instead and leaves precaching empty.

mus2mid moves from example_implementation to the shared src/include trees.
It is a pure data transformation with no SDL dependency, and both the
example and this module now use it; its one example-only include moves
under the STANDALONE guard it belongs to.

Verified by building the module and driving it for 60 ticks plus twenty
fire presses: 26 sounds register with valid DMX headers, `startSound` is
called 111 times, and two songs arrive as MIDI ("MThd"). Building the same
tree with this commit reverted reproduces the released v0.1.0 binary
exactly (sha256 8edfe49a7583fd975199969302d8e9adcf8e714d0af72bf3e672f991fd810faa).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CreYezJ9tefe5BjESSzd7Q
